lesson: 94
title: Saving every week for a price
stars: 0
explain: If you save the same amount every week, the number of weeks is the price divided by the amount saved each week.
explain: A game costs 36 dollars; saving 4 dollars a week, it takes 36 ÷ 4 = 9 weeks.
vars: a=name w=2..12 s=2..15
let: price = w * s
answer: price / s
exercise: {a} saves {s} dollars each week to buy a bike that costs {price} dollars. How many weeks does {a.he} need to save?
exercise: A game costs {price} dollars. {a} puts away {s} dollars every week. How many weeks will it take to have enough?
exercise: {a} wants a kite for {price} dollars. {a.He} saves {s} dollars a week. In how many weeks can {a.he} buy it?
exercise: Every week {a} saves {s} dollars. How many weeks until {a.he} has the {price} dollars for a new bag?
exercise: {a} needs {price} dollars for a ticket and saves {s} dollars each week. How many weeks will {a.he} save?
test: A scooter has a price of {price} dollars. If {a} drops {s} dollars into a jar every week, after how many weeks can {a.he} pay for it?
test: How many weeks must {a} keep saving {s} dollars a week to reach {price} dollars?
test: {a} starts with an empty money box and adds {s} dollars to it once a week. The box must hold {price} dollars for a trip. How many weeks does that take?
test: To pay {price} dollars for a puzzle, {a} saves the same {s} dollars every week. For how many weeks does {a.he} save?
exercise: {a} wants a bike that costs {price} dollars and saves {s} dollars per week. How many weeks will that take?
exercise: How many weeks does it take {a} to save {price} dollars if {a.he} saves {s} dollars a week?
exercise: Price {price} dollars, savings {s} dollars a week. How many weeks are needed?
exercise: {a} lives in Oregon and wants a tent that costs {price} dollars. {a.He} puts {s} dollars aside every week. How many weeks does {a.he} need?
exercise: Each week {a} puts {s} dollars into a piggy bank. A football costs {price} dollars. After how many weeks can {a.he} buy it?
exercise: A pair of skates in Calgary costs {price} dollars. {a} saves {s} dollars every week. How many weeks until {a.he} has enough?
exercise: {a} needs {price} pounds for a school trip to London and saves {s} pounds each week. How many weeks will {a.he} save?
exercise: {a} saves {s.words} dollars every week for a toy that costs {price} dollars. How many weeks does {a.he} save?
test: For how many weeks must {a} save if {a.he} wants {price} dollars and can keep {s} dollars from each week's pocket money?
test: {a}'s goal is a telescope at {price} dollars. With {s} dollars set aside weekly, how many weeks will reaching the goal take?
test: {s} dollars every week, and {a} stops saving when {a.he} has exactly {price} dollars. How many weeks did {a.he} save?
test: A surfboard in Perth costs {price} dollars. {a} puts {s} dollars into a savings account each week. How many weeks until {a.he} can pay for it?
test: How long, in weeks, until {a}'s jar holds {price} dollars, if {a.he} adds {s} dollars once a week?
test: {a} wants to buy a guitar priced {price} dollars and earns {s} dollars a week walking dogs, saving all of it. How many weeks does {a.he} need?
exercise: {a} saving {s} bucks a week for a {price} dollar bike. how many weeks
exercise: game's {price} dollars, puttin away {s+1} a week — no, {s} a week. how many weeks till i can get it
exercise: {a} says it's {price} weeks for a {price} dollar kite at {s} a week lol. nah, how many weeks really
exercise: {s} dollars every week, it's {a}'s birthday in 3 weeks btw, wants a {price} dollar game, how many weeks saving
test: how long till {a} got {price} dollars if {a.he} puts by {s} each week, in weeks
test: {price} dollar scooter, {s+2} — sorry, {s} dollars a week saved. weeks?
test: {a} worked out {price+s} weeks. that right? {price} dollars at {s} a week, how many weeks
exam: It is given that {a} sets aside {s} dollars per week towards a bicycle priced at {price} dollars. Determine the number of weeks required to accumulate the full price.
exam: Ascertain the number of weeks of saving necessary for {a}, who deposits {s} dollars weekly, to attain the sum of {price} dollars.
exam: Whereas an article is priced at {price} dollars and the weekly savings of {a} amount to {s} dollars, state the period, in weeks, required for its purchase.
exam: Compute the duration in weeks over which savings of {s.words} dollars per week will total exactly {price} dollars.
exercise: Since Mum was made redundant, {a} saves {s} dollars a week on {a.his} own for a bike that costs {price} dollars. How many weeks does {a.he} need?
exercise: {a}'s old bike finally gave up the ghost. A new one costs {price} dollars, and {a.he} saves {s} dollars every week. How many weeks until {a.he} can buy it?
test: i'm hard up, all right? game's {price} quid and i can put away {s} a week. how many weeks, and don't tell mum
